rnative release triggers before attributing a wakeup duty.',source_ids=['s-config','s-response-commit','s-read-release'],high_consequence=False),dict(entry_point='RawNode.readyWithoutAccept synchronous Messages publication',disposition='deferred',reason='doc.go permits sending messages while entries in the same batch persist, while rawnode.go states Ready requires persistence before sending. Determine actual Ready/Node contracts and whether response publication needs stricter host ordering.',source_ids=['s-host-contract','s-ready','s-send'],high_consequence=True)],core_overview=dict(status='incomplete',formation=dict(explanation='Leader proposals receive term/index, append to the log and queue a persistence-delayed self acknowledgment. Peer acknowledgments update progress; tracker aggregates current voters using both majorities for joint configuration, then maybeCommit checks the current log term before advancing commitment. Acknowledgment-driven advancement broadcasts append and releases queued reads, while configuration-driven advancement broadcasts without that release.',behavior_ids=['b-commit','b-ready'],fact_ids=['f-current-term-commit'],source_ids=['s-commit-reset','s-response-commit','s-config','s-tracker-commit','s-joint']),context=dict(explanation='Campaign transitions establish candidate term and self vote; vote eligibility uses local vote/leader context and log freshness. PreVote leaves term and vote unchanged. Step handles message terms before role handlers, with explicit pre-vote/lease exceptions and lower-term rejection. Role reset clears accumulated progress and readOnly context while preserving the committed prefix.',behavior_ids=['b-context'],source_ids=['s-authority','s-campaign','s-term','s-voting','s-commit-reset']),connection=dict(explanation='Term dispatch prevents ordinary old responses from becoming new leader support. Persistence-delayed vote/append replies and leader self replies connect durable support to election and commit decisions. Configuration application reinterprets peer progress through a changed voter set and may itself advance commitment; established committed history constrains snapshots and subsequent log repair.',behavior_ids=['b-context','b-ready','b-commit'],source_ids=['s-term','s-send','s-config','s-restore']),core_gaps=['Trace full vote tally and candidate decision handler, timer and transfer paths.','Trace Node/RawNode caller validation, async storage response construction, committed-entry/application boundaries and startup reconstruction.','Trace configuration transition implementation and recovery callers, not just switchToConfig.'],open_details=['Pending-read release following configuration-driven first current-term commit.','Synchronous persistence/send ordering discrepancy across interface descriptions.'],rationale='Initial source-backed partial backbone retains concrete leads without declaring readiness or a violation.'))\njson.dump(m,open('initial-map.json','w'),indent=2)\ns=dict(action='research',rationale='Preserve the initial two-core-path partial understanding and two sourced discrepancies while required supporting paths remain unread.',sources=sources,map_path='initial-map.json',feedback=dict(ref_ids=['b-commit','b-context','b-ready','s-config','s-ready','s-host-contract'],answered='Commit qualification depends on both current voter aggregation and current-term log matching; follow-up read release differs between acknowledgment and configuration entry paths. Deferred responses link host durability obligations to support consumption.',remaining=m['core_overview']['core_gaps']+m['core_overview']['open_details'],understanding='updated',rationale='These are implementation observations and unresolved contract/history questions, not formal defect evidence.'))\njson.dump(s,open('submission.json','w'),indent=2)\nPY\npython3 build_initial.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
